    "body": "Make the shoulder-swap control work while John is in cover. The camera must move to the opposite shoulder from a deliberate button press. The last movement direction can still affect facing, but it must not be the only way to choose the camera side. Resolve the installed cover-state, input, and camera paths before changing code. Preserve ordinary movement and camera controls outside cover. Acceptance: the same shoulder-swap button alternates camera side in left and right cover, John stays attached to cover, aiming remains usable, and leaving cover restores normal camera behavior.",
